# Preserve the exact bytes a reader receives from a clone, on every platform.
# Git's default heuristic rewrites line endings on checkout, so a Windows
# clone with core.autocrlf=true did not reproduce the bytes this project
# tested and published SHA-256 digests for. All paths therefore default to
# byte-preserving checkout; the listed files intentionally opt into text
# normalization and CRLF checkout because CRLF is their tested representation.

* -text

